OrionLayer open fix 101 — a combat command reaches the original's refusal boxes
===============================================================================

Work order 306 (Data, 19 October 2026: "P1 ja. Entscheide die restlichen p
selbst und fix es."). orion2re on the fork's branch `orionlayer` (v2.0.0),
on top of open fix 99; commit 35486477. Not on `orionlayer-local`. In
src/ext/ext_api.cpp, which is built only with ORION2RE_EXT, as the rest of
open fix 58's `Take_Combat_Command`.

Open fix 58's `Take_Combat_Command` refused two commands the original's
click takes and answers with a box (reason 4, nothing shown):

- BOARD at one of the player's own units. The original's click with
  `board_flag` set runs `Initiate_Boarding_Action_` for any live unit
  (combat1.cpp:825-826, the 1.60 source), which refuses an own ship in its
  box: KENTEXT 0x40, 0x41 for a captured one, the planet 0x3F
  (:2032-2037, `Warning_Box_` :2086-2090). Now only the acting unit itself
  is refused; any other unit takes open fix 58's two steps (the BOARD
  radio, then the unit's cell) as an enemy does.
- FIRE at a phased enemy (`special_status_flag` 4). The original's click
  says KENTEXT 80 in its box and fires nothing (:797-802). Now the
  target's cell goes to that click; the FIRE's weapon mask is not applied,
  since no shot puts the rows back. A FIRE at an own unit or at an enemy
  in stasis is still refused.

Both boxes reach the client as every box does (MSGB, open fix 29).

